    "answer": {
      "short": "11.",
      "worked": "An odd sum of two primes must contain 2, the only even prime, and an odd prime.\n\nThe smaller odd numbers greater than 3 are all sums of two primes:\n$$\\begin{align*}5&=2+3\\\\7&=2+5\\\\9&=2+7\\end{align*}$$\nFor 11, the other number would be $11-2=9$, which is not prime. Therefore the smallest such odd number is $11$.",
